KG42.register("clusters-5b2632f8a3db081f885ada94",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v142-d-CL004","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","label":"The paper's participant scope and responsibility for own power balance","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"The paper's participant scope and responsibility for own power balance","market_meaning":"Within the paper's scope of jointly calling producers and consumers prosumers, consumers may participate in the LEM, and participants bear responsibility for maintaining their own power balance. The consumer-specific statement and the collective-responsibility statement are both retained.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Interpret the scope of responsibility according to the paper's collective designation; the consumer node is not declared synonymous with the prosumer node that has a supply meaning in the ontology. This procedural candidate does not claim a closed power-balance equation or billing algorithm.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Participation permission and the post-participation responsibility for own balance have independent market meaning. The charging consequences arising from the responsibility are connected in CL005 through a shared reference; settlement decisions are not absorbed here.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies that consumers are included in the paper's participant scope and carries their balance responsibility."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retains the responsibility statement directed at the paper's collective participant category, without collapsing it into the consumer-specific scope."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g03-E10"],"rationale":"The source's collective designation includes consumers among those bearing responsibility for their own balance; the sub-scope responsibility and the collective responsibility are complementary, and no identity mapping between the two participation nodes is established."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G001","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The paper's prosumers include consumers, whereas the existing ontology definition participation.prosumer emphasizes being able to supply local generation. This terminological difference does not prevent this cluster from assembling the procedural responsibility according to the paper's original scope, but it does not authorize ontological equivalence.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R010::V::participation.prosumer","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm the boundaries of the terminology mapping, and have upstream specify the applicable population; retain the two existing nodes and their respective original statements."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G002","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for the collective designation of participants and for own-balance responsibility remains unverified; assembled indicates only that semantic assembly within the stated scope holds.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the source and the participant scope; do not interpret this cluster's status as scientific approval."}]},"rule_refs":["45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R009","45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-8172b6641813aad0","COMP-fc2134ec5ed3e3df"]});
